Op donderdag 17 februari 2022 om 10:44:39 UTC+1 schreef Isabelle Foote:

> Hi there,
>
> I've been using your genomicSEM package for a while now but I noticed there seems to be a change in the most recent package update that I wanted to mention in case it's a bug (it may also be that I have missed something about the new code update but thought I'd check)?
>
> Basically I've noticed 2 things for the userGWAS function that is not an issue with the commonfactorGWAS function.
>
> 1. The output for userGWAS no longer seems to have name columns but now prints as V1-23 whereas before the columns had the same heading names that you say on the wiki.
>
> 2. When I run a 3-factor model and try to save each of the factors requested in the sub argument (here I used: sub=c("F1~SNP", "F2~SNP", "F3~SNP")) then I noticed that the effect estimates for the first factor print across each section of the Rdata output instead of the 3 different factor results appearing like it used to.
> So for example the estimates in CFAGWAS[[1]], CFAGWAS[[2]] and CFAGWAS[[3]] are all identical.
>
> I got around it by running 3 separate GWASs just running one factor in the sub argument at a time but I wanted to know whether there's a code change that I should be doing on the most recent version?
>
> Please see below for my code - I'm running the GWAS as an array job on the cluster for memory reasons but this code always worked for me before the package update (to give some context)
>
> setwd("/data/Wolfson-DepDem-PNU-CIP/SNP_models_GWAS_noAD")
>
> SGE_TASK_ID <- Sys.getenv('SGE_TASK_ID')
> read_file_name  <- paste0("prepared_sumstats_redo_subset", SGE_TASK_ID, ".txt")
> write_file_name <- paste0("CFA_GWAS_noADorSBP_redo", SGE_TASK_ID, ".Rdata")
>
> # Load packages required
> library(devtools)
> library(GenomicSEM)
>
> # Step 1: Load LDSC output file
> setwd("/data/Wolfson-DepDem-PNU-CIP/SNP_models_GWAS_noAD")
> load("LDSC_FOR_GWAS_SUMSTATS_NO_AD_NOSBP.RData")
>
> ### Step 2: Load in the split summary statistics files (see script for making sumstats file)
>
> CFA_sumstats_redo <- read.table(read_file_name, header = T, sep = "", check.names = F)
>
>
> # STEP 3: Specify the model for the GWAS
> CFA_model <- "F1 =~ V1 + V2 + V3 + V4
> F2 =~ V5 + V4 + V2 + V6 + V7 + V8
> F3 =~ V9 + V10 + V11 + V12
> F1 ~~ F2
> F2 ~~ F3
> F3 ~~ F1
> F1 ~ SNP
> F2 ~ SNP
> F3 ~ SNP"
>
> #STEP 4: run the multivariate GWAS using serial processing and as an array so that all the sumstats files complete in different jobs
> CFA_GWAS_redo <- userGWAS(covstruc = LDSCoutput, SNPs = CFA_sumstats_redo,
>                                estimation = "DWLS", model = CFA_model,
>                                printwarn = TRUE,
>                                sub=c("F1~SNP","F2~SNP","F3~SNP"),
>                                toler = FALSE, SNPSE = FALSE, parallel = FALSE,
>                                cores = NULL, GC="standard", MPI=FALSE, smooth_check=FALSE)
>
> save(CFA_GWAS_redo, file= write_file_name)
>
> Thanks very much!!
> Best wishes
>
> Isabelle

